#17521
Thousand Mile Road~
You crest the ridge and halt abruptly.  The long road has come to an end at the
edge of a rocky cliff.  Heavy brush does not obscure your view of a
breathtaking vista.  Before you is a vast sparking blue expanse of ocean
stretching west north and south as far as the eye can see.  The sharp tang of
salt is on the breeze and the gentle crash of waves is punctuated by the
screech of sea birds soaring on the air currents.  At the edge of the cliff you
peer down and see the rock walls descending to a pebbled beach far below.    
~
