#17572
Thousand Mile Road~
The farmland has now given way to salt marshes lining either side of the road.
The water is brackish and gives off that unmistakeable reek of shoreline.  
Over head gulls soar in lazy circles, their cries stirring your blood for the
gulls mean the ocean is near and with every new ocean comes new lands on the
other side.    
